 CLEAN LRC RESULT (this thread -> a theorem-shaped statement):
   For n-1 distinct gcd-1 speeds, the LRC max-collar M(S) satisfies
        M(S) = 1/n  (only the AP-tight family)   OR   M(S) >= 2/(2n-1).
   i.e. a SPECTRAL GAP of width margin(n)=1/(n(2n-1)) ~ 1/(2n^2) just
   above the conjectured floor 1/n. The AP is isolated: every non-tight
   config clears the LRC bound with a definite surplus >= 1/(n(2n-1)).
   This is exactly the 'how hard is LRC at n' quantity: the difficulty
   is concentrated entirely in the tiny tight family; the bulk clears.
